      "id": "lpic2-lvm-filter-policy",
      "version": 1,
      "track": "LPIC-2",
      "topic": "LVM device selection",
      "unit": "lvm-device-selection",
      "title": "Repair a filter that hides application PVs",
      "summary": "Repair filter ordering and exclude unrelated storage across two supplied inventories.",
      "objective": "Allow /dev/data-main and /dev/data-spare whenever present in either supplied inventory. Exclude every other supplied device, including similar longer names and unrelated arrivals. Use the filter policy; no devices file is supplied in these checks. Save configuration, Run scan, then Check answers. Leave no unsaved edits. Keep all supplied virtual storage and metadata unchanged.",
      "retry_guidance": "Read each failing inventory and path separately. Unsaved edits do not affect a scan. Save the repaired policy, Run scan again, and compare the actual selection mechanism and device results.",
      "difficulty": "Intermediate",
      "minutes": 24,
      "steps": [
        "Inspect the supplied policy and inventories",
        "Repair and save the configuration",
        "Run the actual simulated scan",
        "Check every requirement and repair any mistakes"
      ],
      "guide": [],
      "explanation": "The leading catch-all rejection prevented later accept rules from being reached. Specific whole-path accept rules followed by a final rejection allow both required PVs when present. End anchors prevent longer lookalike names from passing, and the final rejection excludes unrelated arrivals instead of relying on the permissive unmatched default.",
      "hints": [
        "Read which rule matches first for a required PV. A later accept cannot undo an earlier rejection.",
        "Each intended whole-path accept must appear before the catch-all rejection. The ^ and $ anchors distinguish exact names from longer lookalikes.",
        "Unmatched paths are allowed. Keep an explicit final rejection and verify the supplied arrival check too."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://www.lpi.org/our-certifications/exam-201-202-objectives/#rdp-we-204.3_Logical_Volume_Manager_(weight:_3)",
