          "lesson": {
            "prerequisite_note": "Build on the previous LVM inventory and application-reference lessons. A PV is storage prepared for LVM; this unit changes only which supplied virtual metadata is inspected. No storage is formatted, renamed or mounted.",
            "concepts": [
              {
                "title": "Choose which devices LVM may inspect",
                "text": "A physical volume, or PV, is a device prepared for LVM. This exercise reads only supplied virtual metadata. A filter selects paths before their PV labels are inspected; an allowed path may still contain no LVM label."
              },
              {
                "title": "Read one filter rule",
                "text": "The devices section contains a filter array: an ordered list in square brackets. Each quoted entry begins with a to accept or r to reject. In a|^/dev/demo-fast$|, the bars delimit the pattern. ^ means start and $ means end, so the whole supplied path must match. Separate accept entries are valid; you need not combine them into a complicated expression."
              },
              {
                "title": "Put specific matches before the catch-all",
                "text": "LVM uses the first matching rule for each supplied path. A leading r|.*| rejects every path before later accept entries can help. Put the specific accept rules first. A final r|.*| rejects everything else. Without a matching rule, paths are allowed, so leaving out the final rejection is a real policy mistake."
              },
              {
                "title": "Check a second inventory",
                "text": "The example scans its current inventory and a supplied arrival check. The second includes a backup PV and an unrelated device. A filter that handles only the first inventory is incomplete. No devices file is supplied, so this example uses filters; an enabled, present devices file would take precedence."
              }
            ],
            "description": "Allow /dev/demo-fast and /dev/demo-backup when present. Exclude the USB device, the similar longer name and the unrelated arrival. The specific accept rules must win before the final rejection.",
