          "lesson": {
            "prerequisite_note": "Build on the previous LVM inventory and application-reference lessons. A PV is storage prepared for LVM; this unit changes only which supplied virtual metadata is inspected. No storage is formatted, renamed or mounted.",
            "concepts": [
              {
                "title": "Two ways to choose devices",
                "text": "A filter selects paths with ordered accept/reject rules. An enabled devices file instead lists the devices LVM may use. When that file is present and use_devicesfile = 1, its selection takes precedence and the filter is ignored. Do not disable the file merely to hide an incomplete handover."
              },
              {
                "title": "Read the switch and the actual scan mode",
                "text": "In devices { ... }, use_devicesfile = 0 explicitly selects filters. A value of 1 enables a provided devices file. This task supplies that file and requires it to remain in use. A missing file would fall back to filters; a present but empty file would select no devices."
              },
              {
                "title": "Repair the provided selection",
                "text": "The native table below models which supplied devnames are listed. Include the example primary and standby PVs; exclude its imported copy and USB device. Save configuration stores the switch. Save device selection stores membership. Typing or ticking a box alone does not change what a scan reads."
              },
              {
                "title": "Separate selection from metadata",
                "text": "Run scan reads the saved policy against two supplied inventories. Allowed means the selection permits inspection; PV label read describes the actual virtual metadata found. Real system.devices stores hardware IDs and is normally managed by lvmdevices. This table is a disclosed devname-only simulator, not that real file format."
              }
